      "id": "least_squares.split_score",
      "role": "method_property",
      "statement": "For any coefficients the weighted squared error equals c - 2 beta.b + beta.A beta from the rows' summed statistics; the statistics of disjoint row sets add, so prefix sums score every cut; separately minimised sides never exceed the parent's error at shared coefficients (with ridge terms, by at most their penalty on the shared coefficients); and the BIC gate accepts a split exactly when its error is below the parent's times exp(-penalty / n_eff), so never when the error does not fall.",
